//? Title: Nearest-Neighbour TSP

\toc

> Algorithm

From the current city, repeatedly visit the closest unvisited city, then
return to the start.  The invariant is that the partial route contains each
selected city once; termination therefore yields a Hamiltonian cycle.

```
tour <- start
while an unvisited city remains: append the nearest one
append start
```

The direct scan costs \(O(n^2)\).  It is fast but greedy and has no constant
approximation ratio on arbitrary instances.

> C\+\+ example

```{cpp, results="output", exports="both", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/algorithms/tour_search.hpp>
#include <iostream>
int main(){auto r=datamunge::algorithms::nearest_neighbor_tsp(
{{0,1,2},{1,0,1},{2,1,0}});std::cout<<r.cost;}
```
// result_begin:
// 4
// result_end

It returns the three-city cycle of cost 4.
